<title>UK: Russia sets $2.0 billion 10-year bond, 375 bp over.</title>
<headline>Russia sets $2.0 billion 10-year bond, 375 bp over.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers J.P. Morgan Securities and SBC Warburg.</p>
<p> BORROWER   RUSSIA</p>
<p> AMT	  $2.0 BLN  COUPON     10.00     MATURITY    26.JUN.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    26.JUN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  =	   REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+375 BP</p>
<p> NOTES    **TO BE PRICED LATER</p>
<p> MOODY	BA2	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  BB-	 DENOMS (K) 1-10    SALE LIMITS US/GB/FR/RU</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  RUSSIA    TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.625     SELL CONC  0.50	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.625 PCT U.S. T-NOTE DUE 15.MAY.07</p>
<p> NOTES	PRICING DUE AROUND 1315 GMT</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
